## 4. Defects, ranked

No blocker. Players can start, play and finish 1-1 on build-1.

### Major

**D1 — A standing jump does not reach the top of a 4-tile pipe.** *Observed* (feel measurement): small Mario standing on the ground and holding A reaches a 62 px apex; a 4-tile pipe is 64 px. With any horizontal speed (walk jump 66 px, run jump 77.5 px) it works, so the player has to take a step before jumping. *Assumed:* in SMB1 a full standing jump lands on a 4-tile pipe, so this is a feel deviation that will catch players at the two 4-high pipes (tiles ~46 and ~57) and reads as "the jump is weak". qa filed the same measurement in `game-developer#7`. Repro: `python3 tools/measure_feel.py <build> <out>`, key `jump_stand_hold`; real play: stand next to the third pipe and press and hold A. Evidence `evidence/feel/feel.json`. Owner: game-developer.

### Minor

**D2 — 39 asset 404s.** On every load the page requests tile PNGs that do not exist (`assets/tiles/castle/*` such as `flag_ball.png`, `flag_pole.png`, `pipe_l.png`, `pipe_r.png`, `pipe_side_body_b.png`, and underground tile files). The game falls back and 1-1 and the coin room look right, so nothing is visible, but the console is full of red errors and the underground/castle sets are not really delivered yet. `evidence/enemies/probes_enemies.json` (`failed_requests`), `run01/log.json`. Owner: artist/game-developer (already tracked in `artist#3`).

**D3 — A key tap shorter than one logic frame is lost.** Input is sampled once per frame, so a key down and up inside 16.7 ms is never seen. Humans cannot do that, so it did not affect the real-time run; it makes scripted tests flaky (`keyboard.press` needs `delay=80`). Already `game-developer#8`. Owner: game-developer.

### Polish / unverified

**D4 — Small windows.** In a viewport smaller than 256×240 the canvas is not scaled down and is cut off (320×200: 20 px lost top and bottom). On phones the game is a 1× picture in the middle of the screen with no touch controls (the brief says touch is not required). `viewport/vp_320x200_dpr1.png`, `vp_390x844_dpr3.png`.

**D5 — Control hint on the title is drawn over the brick row**, white text on brick tiles, hard to read. `run01/01_title.png`.

**D6 — Wording after the castle**: the clear screen says "YOU CLEARED WORLD 1" although only 1-1 exists in build-1. `win1/win1_02195_clearscreen_fireworks.png`. (build-2's notes say this screen is intended for now; it will need a change when 1-2 exists.)

**D7 — Multi-coin brick pays 12 coins when hit every 22 frames** (`misc/probes_misc.json`, `multi_coin_tight`). *Assumed* SMB1 stops at 10 for a typical player; with the hit cadence a human can manage (the slow test, a hit every 90 frames, gave 4 coins before the brick turned used) I did not see anything wrong. Unverified; do not act without a better reference.

### Notes (not defects)

- Fire Mario shrinks directly to small when hit (SMB1 does the same).
- Fireworks only on 1/3/6 (SMB1 does the same).
- Dev-only: the `stomp` entry in `SMB.game.events` has its `type` overwritten by the enemy type, so tests cannot filter on it; scores were used instead.

